1. ✅ Functional Testing (Core)
Correct request → correct response
All endpoints working as expected
HTTP status codes (200, 400, 401, 500 etc.)

👉 If this fails, nothing else matters.

2. 📦 Response Validation
Response data is correct (not just success=true)
Field values match expected logic
No missing or extra fields
3. 🧱 Schema Validation
JSON structure is consistent
Data types are correct (string, int, boolean)
Required fields always present
4. ❌ Negative Testing (Most people skip this — big mistake)
Invalid inputs (wrong data types)
Missing parameters
Wrong formats (email, phone, etc.)
Check proper error messages

👉 This is where real bugs hide.

5. 🔐 Authentication & Authorization
API works only with valid token
Invalid/expired token → should fail
Role-based access (user vs admin)
6. 🔗 Integration Testing
API works properly with:
Database
Other services
Third-party APIs

👉 Example: Payment success → DB updated? User status changed?

7. 🔁 Regression Testing
Old APIs still working after new release
No existing flows broken
8. 🧪 Edge Cases
Empty values
Large payloads
Boundary values (min/max limits)
9. ⚡ Performance Basic Check (at least minimal)
Response time acceptable (<2–3 sec ideally)
API not timing out
10. 🗄️ Data Validation (Important for your product)
API response = actual DB data
No mismatch or stale data
